    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:2e780f63f4172747",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ae8fe0e276de2569d0f46841a6eef49e2fe93a083ca76cb7a81497301e4f9371",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-0a822c5ae0173752",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, we leave San Juan for Valle Fértil. On arrival, transfer to the hotel and check in.\n\nIn the afternoon, we visit Ischigualasto Park, also known as Argentina’s Valley of the Moon. The park is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and lies at about 1,300 m above sea level.\n\nMost of the park is desert, with cacti, shrubs and small trees.\n\nThe park is particularly important for its palaeontological finds. Fossilised remains of ancient animals and dinosaurs dating back around 180 million years have been found here.\n\nAfter walking through and exploring the park, we return to the hotel for dinner.\n\n**Meals:** Breakfast and dinner."
    },
